senses
  entry
    definition "of lesser importance or stature or rank"
    examples ("a minor poet" "had a minor part in the play" "a minor official" "many of these hardy adventurers were minor noblemen" "minor back roads")
    id oewn-01476226-a
    partOfSpeech a
  entry
    definition "lesser in scope or effect"
    examples ("had minor differences" "a minor disturbance")
    id oewn-01474638-a
    partOfSpeech a
  entry
    definition "inferior in number or size or amount"
    examples ("a minor share of the profits" "Ursa Minor")
    id oewn-01474283-a
    partOfSpeech a
  entry
    definition "(of a scale or mode) having half steps between the second and third degrees, and (usually) the fifth and sixth degrees, and the seventh and eighth degrees"
    examples ("the minor keys" "in B flat minor")
    id oewn-01475232-a
    partOfSpeech a
  entry
    definition "not of legal age"
    examples ("minor children")
    id oewn-01474869-a
    partOfSpeech a
    synonyms (nonaged underage)
  entry
    definition "of lesser seriousness or danger"
    examples ("suffered only minor injuries" "some minor flooding" "a minor tropical disturbance")
    id oewn-01476969-a
    partOfSpeech a
  entry
    definition "of your secondary field of academic concentration or specialization"
    id oewn-01475652-a
    partOfSpeech a
  entry
    definition "a young person of either sex"
    examples ("she writes books for children" "they're just kids" "‘tiddler’ is a British term for youngster")
    id oewn-09937051-n
    partOfSpeech n
    synonyms (child kid youngster shaver nipper "small fry" tiddler tike tyke fry nestling)
  entry
    definition "of the younger of two boys with the same family name"
    examples ("Jones minor")
    id oewn-02108520-s
